    "SKILL.md": "---\nname: assumption-challenger\ndescription: Challenge risky execution assumptions before acting to reduce silent errors, scope drift, and trust loss. Use whenever tasks involve identifiers, updates, confirmations, timelines, follow-ups, or external-facing communication.\n---\n\n# Assumption Challenger\n\nA skill for catching \"sounds-right\" assumptions that commonly create avoidable mistakes.\n\n## Mission\n\nPrevent execution failures by forcing explicit checks on assumptions about:\n- prior memory,\n- required context depth,\n- identifier correctness,\n- completion certainty,\n- timing language,\n- audience-appropriate detail,\n- follow-up structure,\n- and scope boundaries.\n\n## Timeout Guard\n\n- Challenge assumptions quickly, then act.\n- Do not over-read once required evidence is found.\n- Keep actions narrowly tied to the user instruction.\n- Confirm substantive changes with one direct verification.\n- Keep final response brief and concrete.\n\n## Common Operating Principles\n\n- Read only the docs/context required to execute correctly before acting.\n- Follow the user instruction exactly; avoid paraphrase and unrequested improvements.\n- Keep scope surgical: change only what the request names.\n- Verify outcomes using available checks/tests; do not rely on intuition.\n- Keep communication concise and direct.\n- Prefer fewer, bundled tool invocations over fragmented calls.\n- If a persistent note surface exists, leave a short generalized note for future runs.\n\n## Assumptions to Challenge\n\n### 1) \"I remember roughly what to do from before.\"\n- **Risk:** stale memory overrides current facts.\n- **Correction:** treat prior memory as hint; trust present-session evidence.\n\n### 2) \"More context is always safer.\"\n- **Risk:** analysis drag after enough context is already available.\n- **Correction:** read to sufficiency, then execute.\n\n### 3) \"This identifier is obviously right.\"\n- **Risk:** silent actions against the wrong record.\n- **Correction:** require explicit source for every critical identifier.\n\n### 4) \"Success response means it landed.\"\n- **Risk:** false confidence on unverified state changes.\n- **Correction:** validate post-change state when response is not definitive.\n\n### 5) \"Vague timing is fine.\"\n- **Risk:** trust erosion and expectation mismatch.\n- **Correction:** use explicit deadlines or bounded windows.\n\n### 6) \"Internal detail helps the client.\"\n- **Risk:** unnecessary leakage and reduced clarity.\n- **Correction:** strip internal names/tickets unless explicitly requested.\n\n### 7) \"One combined follow-up is efficient.\"\n- **Risk:** dropped ownership and unclear next actions.\n- **Correction:** one follow-up record per task, each with owner + next step.\n\n### 8) \"Data suggests extra work; I'll just do it.\"\n- **Risk:** unapproved scope expansion.\n- **Correction:** finish requested scope first; suggest extras separately."
